                <head>No. 709<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>On May 28 the Soviet Government announced the dissolution of the Soviet Control
                    Commission in the German Democratic Republic and its replacement by a Soviet
                    High Commissioner. The Chairman of the Control Commission, General Chuikov, remained in the country as Commander
                    of the Soviet Occupation Forces. His former political adviser, Vladimir Semyenov, became the new Soviet High
                    Commissioner.</p>
                <p>On the same day, according to despatch 1023 from Berlin, June 3, the Council of
                    Ministers of the German Democratic Republic decreed an increase, effective June
                    30, of an average of 10 percent in the work norms of all important industries.
                    (762B.00/6–353)</p>
            </div>
